==============================================================================================================
PART 1 -- SYMBOLIC (sympy): pole ladder of the continued weight; Watson-lemma edge power law
==============================================================================================================
  den-factor zero  q^(Delta+k) e^(i(theta-theta_v)) = 1  ->  theta = [(2*atan(tan(theta_v/2)),)]
  E_pole = cos(theta_v - i u) = cos(theta_v)*cosh(u) + i(sin(theta_v)*sinh(u))   [u=(Delta+k)lambda]
   -> CENTER theta_v=pi/2: E_pole = I*sinh(u)  (PURELY IMAGINARY ladder)
   -> EDGE theta_v=pi-eps:  Re E_pole = -cos(epsilon)*cosh(u),  Im E_pole = sin(epsilon)*sinh(u)
      omega_pole = E_pole - E_vac: Re = cos(eps)(1-cosh u) < omega_min = cos(eps)-1 (below the support
      floor) EXACTLY when cosh(u) > sec(eps): poles NOT swept; threshold sin(eps_c/2)/sqrt(cos eps_c)
      = sinh(Delta*lambda/2), i.e. eps_c ~ 2 asin(sinh(Delta*lambda/2)) ~ Delta*lambda to O(eps^3).
  Watson lemma: int_0^oo sqrt(w) e^(-s w) dw = sqrt(pi)/(2*s**(3/2));  s -> i t  =>  |G_edge(t)| ~ (sqrt(pi)/2) C t^(-3/2)
  -> the banked sqrt soft edge s_E=1/2 FORCES the edge late-time power t^-(s_E+1) = t^-3/2 ('Airy-class',
     the falloff agentR pre-registered as the alternative to a QNM ladder). Half-integer endpoint series
     w ~ w^(1/2)(h0 + h1 w^(1/2) + ...) -> corrections t^(-2), t^(-5/2), ... (checked numerically, PART 4).

==============================================================================================================
PART 2 -- THE dS TARGETS (pinned): static-patch QNM ladders, both dimensional matchings
==============================================================================================================
  dS_D scalar QNMs [Lopez-Ortega gr-qc/0605027; dS3: Jafferis et al 1305.5523]:
     omega_{n,l} = -i H (2n + l + Delta_pm),   Delta_pm = (D-1)/2 +- sqrt((D-1)^2/4 - m^2/H^2)
     => with N=2n+l: omega_N = -i H (Delta + N): PURELY IMAGINARY, spacing H (Delta-independent),
        offset Delta (probe-dependent), nonzero rate (thermal horizon, T_dS = H/2pi, Gibbons-Hawking 1977).
       dS3 conformal scalar (m^2=3/4 H^2): Delta_+ = 3/2, Delta_- = 1/2;  ladder -i(Delta_pm + N)H
                             dS3 massless: Delta_+ = 2, Delta_- = 0;  ladder -i(Delta_pm + N)H
                             dS2 massless: Delta_+ = 1, Delta_- = 0;  ladder -i(Delta_pm + N)H
                         dS2 m^2=3/16 H^2: Delta_+ = 3/4, Delta_- = 1/4;  ladder -i(Delta_pm + N)H
  MATCHING (a) dS3/center [Marini-Qi-H.Verlinde 2604.21014: dS3 boundary Green fn = (DSSYK 2pt)^2]:
     G(t) must carry ladder (Delta+n)H_eff so that G^2 carries (Delta_3+N)H_eff with Delta_3=2Delta.
  MATCHING (b) dS2-JT/edge [Okuyama 2505.08116; near-dS2 Maldacena-Turiaci-Yang 1904.01911]:
     G(t) must itself carry a ladder (Delta+n)H_eff.
  => the four STRUCTURAL requirements R1-R4 (header) are the SAME under both matchings; only the
     numerical value of H_eff differs. A structural failure kills the placement in EITHER dimension --
     this is how the apples-to-apples caveat is handled without choosing a camp's bulk.

